","scope_step_ids":[],"statement":"An integer n is even if n=2k for some integer k.","step_ids":[],"tool_ids":[]},{"basis":"standard_result","basis_reference":"Parity dichotomy: every integer is either even or of the form 2k+1; applied in steps parity-a and parity-b.","citations":[],"critical":false,"depends_on":[],"discharged_by_step_ids":[],"id":"parity-dichotomy","kind":"deduction","scope_step_ids":[],"statement":"Every integer is even or is of the form 2k+1 for some integer k.","step_ids":["parity-a","parity-b"],"tool_ids":[]},{"basis":"local_assumption","basis_reference":"Temporary negation of the intended irrationality conclusion.","citations":[],"critical":true,"depends_on":[],"discharged_by_step_ids":["lowest-terms-conflict"],"id":"lowest-terms-assumption","kind":"assumption","scope_step_ids":["square-equation","a-square-even","parity-a","substitute-a","b-square-even","parity-b","lowest-terms-conflict"],"statement":"Assume that integers a and b, with b nonzero and no common divisor greater than 1, satisfy sqrt(2)=a/b.","step_ids":[],"tool_ids":[]},{"basis":"derivation","basis_reference":"Derived by squaring the temporary representation and using the definition of sqrt(2).","citations":[],"critical":true,"depends_on":["lowest-terms-assumption","root-definition"],"discharged_by_step_ids":[],"id":"squared-equation","kind":"deduction","scope_step_ids":[],"statement":"Under the temporary assumption, a^2=2b^2.","step_ids":["square-equation"],"tool_ids":[]},{"basis":"derivation","basis_reference":"Derived from the squared equation and the parity dichotomy.","citations":[],"critical":true,"depends_on":["squared-equation","parity-dichotomy"],"discharged_by_step_ids":[],"id":"a-is-even","kind":"deduction","scope_step_ids":[],"statement":"Under the temporary assumption, a is even.","step_ids":["a-square-even","parity-a"],"tool_ids":[]},{"basis":"derivation","basis_reference":"Derived by substituting the even form of a and applying the parity dichotomy to b.","citations":[],"critical":true,"depends_on":["squared-equation","a-is-even","parity-dichotomy"],"discharged_by_step_ids":[],"id":"b-is-even","kind":"deduction","scope_step_ids":[],"statement":"Under the temporary assumption, b is even.","step_ids":["substitute-a","b-square-even","parity-b"],"tool_ids":[]},{"basis":"derivation","basis_reference":"Both-evenness contradicts the temporary lowest-terms assumption.","citations":[],"critical":true,"depends_on":["lowest-terms-assumption","a-is-even","b-is-even"],"discharged_by_step_ids":[],"id":"lowest-terms-contradiction","kind":"deduction","scope_step_ids":[],"statement":"The temporary lowest-terms representation is impossible.","step_ids":["lowest-terms-conflict"],"tool_ids":[]},{"basis":"derivation","basis_reference":"Reductio: the contradiction discharges the temporary assumption.","citations":[],"critical":true,"depends_on":["lowest-terms-assumption","lowest-terms-contradiction"],"discharged_by_step_ids":[],"id":"irrationality-conclusion","kind":"deduction","scope_step_ids":[],"statement":"sqrt(2) is irrational.","step_ids":["lowest-terms-conflict","conclude-irrational"],"tool_ids":[]}],"open_questions":[],"proof_steps":[{"citations":[],"depends_on":[],"id":"square-equation","justification":"Square sqrt(2)=a/b, use (sqrt(2))^2=2, and multiply by b^2; b is nonzero by the temporary assumption.","statement":"Derive a^2=2b^2."},{"citations":[],"depends_on":["square-equation"],"id":"a-square-even","justification":"The right-hand side 2b^2 is divisible by 2.","statement":"a^2 is even."},{"citations":[],"depends_on":["a-square-even"],"id":"parity-a","justification":"Apply parity dichotomy to a. If a=2k+1, then a^2=4k^2+4k+1=2(2k^2+2k)+1, which is odd, contradicting step a-square-even. Hence a is even.","statement":"There is an integer c such that a=2c."},{"citations":[],"depends_on":["square-equation","parity-a"],"id":"substitute-a","justification":"Substitute a=2c into a^2=2b^2 to obtain 4c^2=2b^2, then divide by 2.","statement":"b^2